# cuts/v1.0.25/cut.env -- the pins bin/rollforward_gate.sh binds for --cut v1.0.25
#
# The gate reads exactly TWO keys, and the mapping is DECLARED in the runner:
#     OSTLER_PIN_OA="$(_cut_pin DAEMON_COMMIT)"
#     OSTLER_PIN_CM051="$(_cut_pin CM051)"
# Everything else is prose the gate never touches. Keep it that way: the v1.0.24
# attempt to vendor OS003's fuller records dragged 464 lines of operator working
# notes, four private box IPs and five notarisation IDs into the product repo.
#
# WHY v1.0.25 EXISTS. v1.0.24's cut never produced a DMG: CI could not fetch the
# daemon because CM051 had no cross-org credential. Fixed on main by #612
# (CM051_RELEASES_READ, fine-grained, ostler-ai/ostler-releases, Contents:Read,
# expires 2026-11-11). A workflow run uses the workflow file from the TAG, not
# from main, so re-running v1.0.24 would have executed the old cut.yml and failed
# identically. This tag is the first that can exercise the wire.

# The daemon this DMG ships. gui/Makefile carries DAEMON_VERSION ?= 0.4.55.
#
# hub-v0.4.55 is an ANNOTATED tag: the ref points at tag object d40c3535 and the
# COMMIT is e0234e71. Pinning the tag object would name a non-commit and every
# ancestry check would fail in a way that reads as a stale daemon rather than a
# malformed pin.
#
# This build carries the fixes for five open rows, each verified by ancestry with
# a discriminating control: D002 (2c974f27), D038 (f78f56b5), D039 (bb71a40e),
# plus D011 and D014c. It is also now the daemon RUNNING on the founder Mini,
# installed 2026-08-13, which is how ~/.ostler/daemon-build.json first appeared.
DAEMON_COMMIT=e0234e71c66d

# CM051 main at tag time -- 45639b98.
#
# It must be a descendant of edff9c9e (#612), or the workflow this tag runs has
# no cross-org token and cannot fetch the daemon. It must also be at or after
# 1eb7dc0b (#613, the 1.0.24 -> 1.0.25 bump), or the tree declares 1.0.24 and
# fails installer version-consistency. Both hold here.
#
# MOVED from 1eb7dc0b on 2026-08-13, and the reason is the whole point of this
# key. #618 type-hardened the two Tailscale JSON parsers INSIDE install.sh, and
# the rollforward gate reads install.sh at this ref:
#
#     repos/<CM051_REPO>/contents/install.sh?ref=$CM051_REF
#
# Leaving the pin at 1eb7dc0b would have gated an install.sh that is not the one
# in the DMG. Measured before the move: `if not isinstance(self_block, dict):`
# appears 2x at 45639b98 and 0x at 1eb7dc0b. A pin that trails a shipped change
# to a gated file asks its question about a product nobody is cutting, which is
# the failure the header of DEFECTS_ROLLFORWARD.md warns about in the other
# direction (pin vs main). Re-point this key whenever a merge lands in a file a
# gate reads.
CM051=45639b98
